preConditionHook:
// "The high or low of the day usually forms in the first hour." Past the
// opening window, the session's low (long side) was made INSIDE that window
// and is still the session low, and price has come back to within nearAtr
// ATRs of it -- so the level can be traded as the probable low of the day.
// Short is the mirror on the session high.
//
// The measurable half of the strict trend-from-the-open definition: the day's
// extreme was set early and has gone unchallenged. Kept apart from
// TrendFromOpenFlag because it fires on DIFFERENT bars -- that flag only
// needs the first bar's extreme taken out, this needs price back NEAR the
// level after the opening window has closed.
//
// loBar / hiBar are the bars-into-session indices at which the running
// extreme was last improved. The comparisons are STRICT, so a tie keeps the
// EARLIER bar -- the convention EL's own Highest/Lowest carry, since they
// bottom out in Extremes and scan strictly.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)); barsIn is 1 on the
// session's first bar, so "inside the opening window" is
// barsIn <= firstHourBars. Intraday bars only.
//
// The ATR block is AtrProfitTarget's WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator,
// one call site in the hook so it advances exactly once per bar; the update
// is TWO statements because EL evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    sessHigh = high[0];
    sessLow = low[0];
    hiBar = 1;
    loBar = 1;
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    if (el_gt(high[0], sessHigh)) {
        sessHigh = high[0];
        hiBar = barsIn;
    }
    if (el_lt(low[0], sessLow)) {
        sessLow = low[0];
        loBar = barsIn;
    }
}
if (atrLen != (int)atrLookback) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLookback; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLen = (int)atrLookback;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLookback;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrv = atrSum / (int)atrLookback;
